From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: kebab refactor <kebab@local.invalid>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 01:42:30 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] net: wwan: expose the Qualcomm remote-EFS MHI channel as a
 port

A phone-embedded SDX55 runs an RMTEFS firmware build: it has no storage
of its own and expects the application processor to host its
filesystem over MHI channel 10/11, the job Android gives to
/vendor/bin/ks.

With nothing bound there, mhi0_EFS exists but nothing services it. The
modem's EFS stays read-only and RAM-backed from the static Sahara
efs{1,2,3}.bin images, its NV -- IMEI, RF calibration -- never
persists, and it ERRFATALs a fixed ~65 s after its first EFS-Sync,
which on this device meant a reproducible death at around 706 s
uptime.

Add WWAN_PORT_EFS and bind the EFS channel to it, so a userspace
daemon can speak the Sahara memory-debug protocol on /dev/wwanXefsY.

NOTE: the port must be kept out of ModemManager's control-port probing
(ID_MM_PORT_IGNORE). AT-probing it makes the modem's rmts_srv receive
the strings as garbage and ERRFATAL within two seconds, which is worse
than not adding the port at all.

This is Qualcomm-specific and not a generic control port, so it is not
proposed as an upstream abstraction as-is; it records the missing
transport requirement.
---
 drivers/net/wwan/mhi_wwan_ctrl.c | 15 +++++++++++++++
 drivers/net/wwan/wwan_core.c     |  4 ++++
 include/linux/wwan.h             |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/net/wwan/mhi_wwan_ctrl.c b/drivers/net/wwan/mhi_wwan_ctrl.c
index a31d8540f..8c0852c7b 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wwan/mhi_wwan_ctrl.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wwan/mhi_wwan_ctrl.c
@@ -263,6 +263,21 @@ static const struct mhi_device_id mhi_wwan_ctrl_match_table[] = {
 	{ .chan = "DIAG", .driver_data = WWAN_PORT_QCDM },
 	{ .chan = "FIREHOSE", .driver_data = WWAN_PORT_FIREHOSE },
 	{ .chan = "NMEA", .driver_data = WWAN_PORT_NMEA },
+	/*
+	 * The phone-embedded SDX55 runs an RMTEFS firmware build: it has no
+	 * storage of its own and expects the AP to host its filesystem over
+	 * MHI channel 10/11 (the job Android gives to /vendor/bin/ks).
+	 * Without a driver bound here, mhi0_EFS exists but nothing services
+	 * it, so the modem's EFS stays read-only and RAM-backed from the
+	 * static Sahara efs{1,2,3}.bin images. It then ERRFATALs a fixed
+	 * ~73 s after its first EFS-Sync, and its NV (IMEI, RF calibration)
+	 * never persists.
+	 *
+	 * Exposing it as a wwan char device lets a userspace daemon speak
+	 * the Sahara memory-debug protocol on it. Not upstreamable as-is:
+	 * EFS is not a generic control port.
+	 */
+	{ .chan = "EFS", .driver_data = WWAN_PORT_EFS },
 	{},
 };
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(mhi, mhi_wwan_ctrl_match_table);
diff --git a/drivers/net/wwan/wwan_core.c b/drivers/net/wwan/wwan_core.c
index ccce2ad74..87d012eb3 100644
--- a/drivers/net/wwan/wwan_core.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wwan/wwan_core.c
@@ -350,6 +350,10 @@ static const struct {
 		.devsuf = "mipc",
 	},
 	/* WWAN_PORT_NMEA is exported via the GNSS subsystem */
+	[WWAN_PORT_EFS] = {
+		.name = "EFS",
+		.devsuf = "efs",
+	},
 };
 
 static ssize_t type_show(struct device *dev, struct device_attribute *attr,
diff --git a/include/linux/wwan.h b/include/linux/wwan.h
index 1e0e2cb53..2527abaf9 100644
--- a/include/linux/wwan.h
+++ b/include/linux/wwan.h
@@ -20,6 +20,7 @@
  * @WWAN_PORT_ADB: ADB protocol control
  * @WWAN_PORT_MIPC: MTK MIPC diagnostic interface
  * @WWAN_PORT_NMEA: embedded GNSS receiver with NMEA output
+ * @WWAN_PORT_EFS: Qcom remote-EFS (Sahara memory-debug) filesystem channel
  *
  * @WWAN_PORT_MAX: Highest supported port types
  * @WWAN_PORT_UNKNOWN: Special value to indicate an unknown port type
@@ -36,6 +37,7 @@ enum wwan_port_type {
 	WWAN_PORT_ADB,
 	WWAN_PORT_MIPC,
 	WWAN_PORT_NMEA,
+	WWAN_PORT_EFS,
 
 	/* Add new port types above this line */
 
